From 3a1f84d39357fa254f98d76f40c3278501e4956f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zybo Pcam 5C port <noreply@local>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 23:20:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: ov5640: fix CSI-2 720p frame period at 30 fps

The CSI-2 720p mode uses a 62 MHz pixel rate, HTS 1600 and VTS 1280.
That produces 30.2734 fps even though the mode advertises 30 fps.  It
also shortens the automatic 60 Hz banding exposure range by one step.

Use VTS 1292 (720 active lines plus 572 lines of vertical blanking).
This produces 29.9923 fps and lets the banding filter use four complete
60 Hz exposure steps.

Changing the mode default is intentional.  Applying VBLANK before the
stream starts is ineffective because the mode programming sequence
writes the default VTS after the controls have been restored.

Signed-off-by: Zybo Pcam 5C port <noreply@local>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
@@ -1040,6 +1040,6 @@ static const struct ov5640_mode_info ov5640_mode_data[OV5640_NUM_MODES] = {
 			},
 			.htot		= 1600,
-			.vblank_def	= 560,
+			.vblank_def	= 572,
 		},
 		.reg_data	= ov5640_setting_720P_1280_720,
 		.reg_data_size	= ARRAY_SIZE(ov5640_setting_720P_1280_720),
-- 
